 "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010777/state.json" "file_sha256" "e39c26b45208628dfd3fc441fcf876c2eee59912cc354b70df3aa44388f5ae56" "basis" 1156 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010777/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-102693" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "17\\,\\text{m/s}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010777/state.json" "file_sha256" "e39c26b45208628dfd3fc441fcf876c2eee59912cc354b70df3aa44388f5ae56" "basis" 1156 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010777/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-102693" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "9\\,\\text{m/s}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010777/state.json" "file_sha256" "e39c26b45208628dfd3fc441fcf876c2eee59912cc354b70df3aa44388f5ae56" "basis" 1156 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010777/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in $\\text{m}/{\\text{s}}^{2},$ given by the function $a(t)=6{t}^{2}-2t-10$, where $t$ is the time in seconds. If the particle has velocity $v=-4\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}$ when $t=1\\,\\text{s}$, calculate the speed of the particle at the moment $t=3\\,\\text{s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010777/state.json" "file_sha256" "e39c26b45208628dfd3fc441fcf876c2eee59912cc354b70df3aa44388f5ae56" "basis" 1156 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010777/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (6{t}^{2}-2t-10)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}-10t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(1)=-4.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4 & =2(1)^{3}-(1)^{2}-10(1)+C \\\\ -4 & =2-1-10+C \\\\ C & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=2{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}-10t+5.$\n\nWe evaluate the velocity at time $t=3\\,\\text{s}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(3) & =2(3)^{3}-(3)^{2}-10(3)+5 \\\\  & =54-9-30+5 \\\\  & =20\\,\\text{m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the speed is equal to $|v(t)|,$ we conclude that the speed of the particle is $20\\,\\text{m/s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010777/state.json" "file_sha256" "e39c26b45208628dfd3fc441fcf876c2eee59912cc354b70df3aa44388f5ae56" "basis" 1156 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010777/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010777/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97bf1afa6ceed68565479fe95947852ea820cfb8ac2cec4ad8694941a33898d7" "basis" 1156 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010777/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81474" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/140